        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><verbatim>embed:rst 
Determines whether the id of some node has no children of its own :raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;` :raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;`

.. note::
   Ported as-is from the pure-Python original&apos;s own ``isChild``, name and all -- despite
   the name, this checks whether &apos;nodeId&apos; has *no entry* in #children (i.e. it&apos;s a leaf/
   token node produced by a shift, as opposed to an internal node produced by reducing a
   production), not whether it appears as some other node&apos;s child
</verbatim></para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>nodeId</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The id of the node</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>Whether &apos;nodeId&apos; exists in <ref refid="class_a_g_remap_core_1_1_parse_tree_1ad90799f246a45a80cf1958885727e0a2" kindref="member">nodes</ref> and has no children of its own </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
